        'data_p_dataset_2' => 'The same dataset also drives %1$s curated %2$s and %3$s hand-written %4$s. The interactive compare tool itself can match up any two of the %5$s researched brokers on demand; %6$s of those pairings -- every combination among our top %7$s by rank -- also get their own indexed, linkable page rather than existing only inside the tool.',
        'data_p_regulator' => '%1$s regulators -- CySEC, FCA, Seychelles FSA, ASIC, FSCA, DFSA, New Zealand\'s FMA, Singapore\'s MAS, and Kenya\'s CMA -- each with its own %2$s: jurisdiction, leverage rules, compensation scheme (or the honest absence of one), complaint process, the official register to check a firm against, and a live roster of which of our researched brokers currently hold that licence. Summed across all nine, our researched brokers hold %3$s confirmed regulatory licences between them -- a broker holding three regulators\' licences counts three times in that total, since the point is to show the real footprint, not a brokers-vs-regulators ratio. Where two regulators are commonly confused with each other -- a broker\'s legal entity, a Tier-1-vs-offshore distinction, a specific compensation cap -- our %4$s covers %5$s directly.',
        'data_p_research' => '%1$s so far, each built entirely from this site\'s own %2$s-broker dataset -- not a third-party survey, not a press release, a direct count of something already in our research. Every report states its own methodology up front: sample size, the date the underlying data was last reviewed, how we define a "confirmed" fact, how missing data is handled, and the source hierarchy used to confirm each figure. See the %3$s. This is a deliberately small, growing library -- a handful of excellent, citable reports, not a mechanically generated one for every possible cross-section of the dataset.',
        'data_p_confidence' => 'Not every fact in this dataset is equally well-sourced, and we don\'t present them as if they were. Individual facts on broker review pages carry a HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW confidence badge computed from the same hedge language our own research notes already use -- "confirmed via the broker\'s own published page" rates differently from "sources disagree" or "not independently confirmed." A fact with no such signal either way is left unrated rather than assigned a guessed middle tier. See any %1$s\'s deep-dive section for this in practice.',
        'data_p_tools' => 'Three interactive tools run directly against the same dataset rather than a separate copy of it: the %1$s (filters our full researched set down to brokers matching your own answers), the %2$s (estimates your own annual spread cost at every broker with a confirmed spread), and the %3$s (the full regulation dossier for any one researched broker). None of the three hold their own separate data -- a change to a broker\'s record updates all three automatically.',
